#: arts.cpp:109
msgid ""
"Unable to start the sound server to retrieve possible sound I/O methods.\n"
"Only automatic detection will be available."
msgstr ""
"Qullanırlıq K/Ç ısulların tanıp alu öçen tawış serveren cibärep bulmí.\n"
"Üzennän sizü genä qullanıp bula."

#: arts.cpp:146
msgid ""
"<h1>Sound System</h1> Here you can configure aRts, KDE's sound server. This "
"program not only allows you to hear your system sounds while simultaneously "
"listening to an MP3 file or playing a game with background music. It also "
"allows you to apply different effects to your system sounds and provides "
"programmers with an easy way to achieve sound support."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Tawış Sisteme</h1> KDE'neñ aRts atlı tawış serveren bonda caylap bula. Bu "
"yazılımnı qullanıp beryulı sistem tawışların da, MP3 uynatuın da, uyınnarnıñ "
"artyaq köyen dä tıñlap bula. Anıñ aşa sistem tawışlarına törle tä'sirlär östäp "
"bula, uyınnarğa tawış totuın da ciñel itep kertep bula."

#: arts.cpp:167
msgid "&General"
msgstr "&Töptän"

#: arts.cpp:168
msgid "&Hardware"
msgstr "&Cıhazlar"

#: arts.cpp:182
msgid ""
"Normally, the sound server defaults to using the device called <b>/dev/dsp</b> "
"for sound output. That should work in most cases. On some systems where devfs "
"is used, however, you may need to use <b>/dev/sound/dsp</b> "
"instead. Other alternatives are things like <b>/dev/dsp0</b> or <b>/dev/dsp1</b>"
", if you have a soundcard that supports multiple outputs, or you have multiple "
"soundcards."
msgstr ""
"Tawış serverendä tawış çığışı öçen töpcay bulıp <b>/dev/dsp</b> "
"digän cıhaz qullanıla. Oçraqlarnıñ kübesendä bu eşlärgä tieş. Sanaqta devfs "
"digän birem sisteme qullanılğan çaqta <b>/dev/sound/dsp</b> "
"cıhazın qullanu kiräklege çığuı bar. Berniçä tawıs kartı quyılğan, yä ki tawış "
"kartınıñ bernıcä çığışı bulğan çaqta <b>/dev/dsp0</b> yä <b>/dev/dsp1</b> "
"kebek cıhazlarnı qullanu kiräklegeneñ bulıp çığuı bar."

#: arts.cpp:184
msgid ""
"Normally, the sound server defaults to using a sampling rate of 44100 Hz (CD "
"quality), which is supported on almost any hardware. If you are using certain "
"<b>Yamaha soundcards</b>, you might need to configure this to 48000 Hz here, if "
"you are using <b>old SoundBlaster cards</b>, like SoundBlaster Pro, you might "
"need to change this to 22050 Hz. All other values are possible, too, and may "
"make sense in certain contexts (i.e. professional studio equipment)."
msgstr ""
"Tawış servereneñ töpcay bulıp 44100 Hz yışlığına ürnäkläw qullanıla (CD kebek), "
"cıhazlarnıñ kübese anı tota. <b>Yamaha tawışkard</b> "
"qullanılğan çaqta bu köylämädä 48000 Hz quyılğan bulırğa tieş, SoundBlaster Pro "
"kebek <b>iske SoundBlaster kartları</b> qullanılsa inde, bu köylämäne 22050 Hz "
"itep üzgärtäse. Başqa köylämälärneñ dä buluı bar, hönärle studio cıhazlarında "
"kebek ayırmalı eşlär öçen."

#: arts.cpp:186
msgid ""
"This configuration module is intended to cover almost every aspect of the aRts "
"sound server that you can configure. However, there are some things which may "
"not be available here, so you can add <b>command line options</b> "
"here which will be passed directly to <b>artsd</b>. The command line options "
"will override the choices made in the GUI. To see the possible choices, open a "
"Konsole window, and type <b>artsd -h</b>."
msgstr ""
"aRts digän tawış server caylawınıñ bar yaqların da bu modul aşa köyläp bula. "
"Bonda tabılmağan köylämälär bulsa da, <b>artsd</b> atlı xezmätkä turıdan "
"tapşırası <b>boyıryul köylämälären</b> bonda bilgeläp bula. Boyıryul aşa "
"kertelgän köylämälär bu caylaw täräzäsennän kertkän cayların almaşıraçaq. Bar "
"bulğan köylämälär kürü öçen, boyıru täräzäsen açıp <b>artsd -h</b> "
"boyırığın kertäse."

